WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.950
Treasure Island

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.180
<i>There's no wind and the fog is thick.</i>

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:10.460
<i>The Hispaniola is immobilized.</i>

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:12.900
<i>It's my first "dead calm".</i>

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.870
<i>Silver and I have taken this opportunity to go out on the sea...</i>

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.260
<i>...and fish for some dinner for the crew.</i>

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:36.420
<i>Fishing was a big success.</i>

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.640
<i>We returned to the Hispaniola in triumph, but...</i>

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.340
It's strange, no one is on guard.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.150
What's more, it's too quiet.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.940
Treasure
Island

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.740
Takarajima

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.550
saa ikou

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.550
Come, let's go

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.640
yume ni mita shima heto

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.640
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:21.480
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:21.480
Across the waves, on the wind

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:24.360
umi hedeyou

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:24.360
We'll travel the oceans

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:27.280
ikute ni wa

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:27.280
Many of us

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:30.280
minna mada shiranai

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:30.280
Still don't know of

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:34.030
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:34.030
The days and nights full of mystery

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.530
matte iru darou

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.530
That await us there

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:40.040
itsumo shinji you

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:40.040
We must always have trust

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:43.290
magokoro wo

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:43.290
And be sincere

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:49.550
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:49.550
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.680
tade hitotsu no

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.680
I only...

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:56.100
akogare dake wa

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:56.100
...have one desire

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.390
doko no dare ni mo

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.390
And no one...

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:05.100
kese wa shinai sa

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:05.100
...will ever take it away

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.650
tade hitotsu no

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.650
I only...

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.950
akogare dake wa

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.950
...have one desire

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.280
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.280
And no one...

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:24.210
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:24.210
...will ever take it away

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:35.130
episode

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:35.130
The Ghost Ship
\h        Is Calling Me!

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:42.260
Please lower your weapon, First Mate Arrow.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.280
What did you say?!

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:47.230
Ever since I boarded this ship,
I haven't been able to understand you.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.960
Your rules, you know what I mean.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:52.230
I'm tired of you acting special!

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.730
And you want me to believe you'll fire?

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:55.640
Shut up!

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:59.420
It's not just me, everyone hates you!

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:00.030
Puppy.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.030
Can you tell me what happened?

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:07.520
It's the first mate,
he's completely lost his mind.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.600
It happened right after you left for fishing.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:16.000
Captain Smollett was astounded when he caught him secretly drinking rum.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.120
<i>First Mate Arrow! I believe I have banned alcohol on board!</i>

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:23.930
<i>You are no longer my first mate.
I've demoted you to an ordinary sailor!</i>

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:27.120
You could say that Mr. Arrow was awfully shocked, too.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.640
Becoming an ordinary sailor, his pay was cut in half.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.520
"Forgive me", he said,
and then he started to cry.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:37.400
But the Captain didn't
want to hear any more.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.900
It's then that First Mate Arrow
completely lost his head.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:44.720
His resentment was just too strong.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:45.870
It can't be helped.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.990
Indeed, it can't be helped.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:51.210
Don't move.

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:54.240
This is no joke.
I'll blow your brains out!

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:57.400
Mr. Arrow, I'll say it again, lower your weapon!

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:02.840
Otherwise, I will have to consider this as an act of mutiny.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:05.140
It's a crime under maritime law.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:09.020
Sh-Shut up!
This is a request, not a mutiny!

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:11.440
A request?!
You must be joking!

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:14.620
I don't consider having a pistol pointed at me a request!

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.940
Come now, Captain.
There's no need to raise your voice.

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:21.740
This man has a request.
Why not listen?

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.960
I will listen when he puts down his weapon.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.660
But before is out of the question!

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:32.250
Wait, Mr. Arrow!
First Mate Arrow!

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.160
I am the owner of this ship.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.000
I will listen to your request on behalf of the Captain.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.380
Go on, I'm listening.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:44.470
H-Hey, wait!

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:47.430
Where are you going at a time like this?

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.760
I'm going back out fishing,

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:52.730
I believe there is a big catch to make.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:56.150
A big catch to make?

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:00.730
Very well. Here is my first request.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:03.150
Go on, go on.
I'm listening.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:06.000
Regarding the situation of my demotion,

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.120
I want you to take back this unjust decision!

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:13.080
Understood, it's done.
What else?

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.520
Secondly,

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:18.040
in case of a "dead calm",
alcohol must be authorized on board!

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:22.600
Way to go, Mr. Arrow!
How nice of you to think of us.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:28.680
See?
I'm thinking of everyone~hic!

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:32.100
And lastly, write and sign this:

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:36.740
"On August 26, negotiations took place aboard the Hispaniola...

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:40.850
...between First Mate Arrow
and Captain Smollett.

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:44.990
I certify by my honour as a gentleman that it did not result in any sort of mutiny."

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:47.990
"My honour as a gentleman."

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:49.450
There, will that do?

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:51.410
Don't forget to sign!

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.400
Oh, yes, I'll sign.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:56.910
John Trelawney, owner of the Hispaniola.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:58.880
There, it's done.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:02.550
Perfect.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.920
With this in hand,

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:07.380
you cannot sue me for this little "dispute".

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.910
And don't forget, Captain.

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:13.350
This was a negotiation between gentlemen.

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:22.020
Silver!

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:44.710
Give it to me, Silver!

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:48.380
Without this piece of paper, it's the noose for me!

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:51.670
You can give it to him, Mr. Silver.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:55.310
I don't have the intention of pursuing Mr. Arrow in justice.

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:59.270
I just hope it won't happen again.

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:09.200
You are more generous
than you seem, Captain.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:15.120
What are you still doing here?!
Return to your posts!

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:24.270
<i>First Mate Arrow's "personal" mutiny...</i>

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:27.670
<i>...ended well thanks to the intervention of Silver.</i>

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:36.190
<i>But as night fell, the fog persisted.</i>

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:38.510
<i>Again we endured the "dead calm".</i>

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:46.070
Have an apple.

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:46.950
Thanks!

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:02.000
Hey, Jim, you were whistling, right?

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:03.910
Y-Yeah.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:07.270
Whistling attracts demons and causes storms.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:13.260
Although this is just a superstition,
we shouldn't whistle on board.

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:20.180
They say some got killed by their fellow sailors,
because the fools were whistling on board.

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:27.350
What it comes down to... At first sight,
sailors seem like hard and violent men,

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:32.230
but in fact, many of them are weaklings who fear superstitions.

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:37.510
Be careful, Jim, the only person on the sea who you can count on is yourself.

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:41.000
<i>I understand.</i>

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:55.890
Say, this is the signature of Mr. Trelawney, right?

00:08:56.510 --> 00:09:00.430
As long as I have this,
I can escape court, right?

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:04.350
Don't you worry.
Nobody wants to send you there.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:05.810
Don't lie to me!

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:09.440
You won't get me like that!

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:14.380
You say that now, but as soon as we get back to the country you'll drag me to the judges!

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:17.620
Isn't that right?
That's what will happen!

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:22.290
I'm done for!

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:24.080
What an idiot.

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:28.250
Now that the effects of alcohol have worn off,
he realizes the severity of his actions.

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:33.910
Oh, right...

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:35.220
Hey, Silver!

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:39.730
I'm sure that we've already met somewhere.

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:42.140
Now, where was it?

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:47.100
You say we've already met, I don't remember.

00:09:47.470 --> 00:09:50.030
No...
I'm sure we've met!

00:09:50.030 --> 00:09:52.790
Geez, I can't remember!

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.230
You've already met?

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:03.470
'Course not.
His memory must be a mess.

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:06.910
I don't know any rambling drunkard like him.

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:10.880
Nighty, Jim.
See you tomorrow.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:12.250
Yup, see you tomorrow!

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:32.730
Sound the alarm!
Man overboard!

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:35.110
What?!
What's that?!

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:39.070
It's Mr. Arrow!
First Mate Arrow has fallen into the sea!

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:42.160
Who, Mr. Arrow?

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:42.160
My God!

00:10:55.970 --> 00:10:57.510
He's dead! He's dead!

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:59.930
Mr. Arrow is dead!
He's dead! He's dead!

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.640
Mr. Arrow is dead!
Dead! Dead!

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.220
Mr. Arrow is dead!

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:06.850
Dead! Dead!

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:10.030
Did anyone see Mr. Arrow fall into the water?

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:13.190
Me, I saw him.

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:16.240
Well, although I say "saw him"...

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:19.170
Truthfully, I didn't really see him fall overboard.

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:20.700
We're listening, Silver.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:22.330
It was earlier.

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:25.930
I was in my bed, but sleep eluded me.

00:11:25.930 --> 00:11:29.810
I went up on deck.
There he was, drinking.

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:32.080
He was standing on the railing.

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:35.000
He looked really drunk.

00:11:35.530 --> 00:11:39.330
He looked like he was about to fall and I thought about warning him.

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:41.440
But because of recent events,

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:44.510
I thought that I must avoid provoking him.

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:48.750
It happened when I was returning to my cabin.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:12:00.650
He was already on the railing.

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:03.610
I suppose he must have slipped.

00:12:09.530 --> 00:12:10.580
It's no use, Captain!

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:14.460
Surely, Mr. Arrow is shark food by now!

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:29.640
<i>In the end, we never found
the body of First Mate Arrow.</i>

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:37.440
What is it, Jim?

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:42.650
It's strange.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:43.410
What is?

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:46.890
First Mate Arrow slipping because he was drunk...

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:48.130
...is very strange.

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:49.950
Why's that?

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:52.710
Because the first mate wasn't drunk at all!

00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:57.850
Remember? When we ate an apple on the deck before bed...

00:12:57.850 --> 00:13:00.890
We met the first mate there, right?

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:05.000
Yes, I remember it well.
He wouldn't stop sobbing.

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:06.180
Exactly.

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:10.010
At the time, though what he said wasn't making any sense,

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:11.920
you even said:

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:13.140
"What an idiot."

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:16.900
"Now that the effects of alcohol have worn off,
he realizes the severity of his actions."

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:26.770
Back there, he wasn't drunk.

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:30.130
Besides, he fell into the sea about an hour later.

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:35.040
First Mate Arrow didn't have time to drink before he fell overboard!

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:43.760
Then maybe it was I who
tossed him into the water.

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:52.850
Listen, Jim. When I saw him I can assure you that he was drunk.

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:54.450
Mr. Arrow was a drunk.

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:58.370
An hour was surely enough time to drink his bottle of rum.

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:01.990
But you are free to believe me or not, Jim.

00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:06.390
Guys, let me through.

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.990
Silver!

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:12.990
I believe you, Silver!

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:43.090
<i>As the wind picked up at dawn,</i>

00:14:43.090 --> 00:14:44.970
<i>the "dead calm" had finally passed.</i>

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:49.070
<i>And not just the wind.
We had rain and lightning as bonus.</i>

00:14:49.730 --> 00:14:52.360
Storm! Storm!
A storm is coming!

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:55.750
A storm!

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:55.750
Hurry!

00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:59.130
Raise the main sail!

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:02.450
We'll profit from this wind and catch up.

00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:05.630
This little storm will not be feared by the Hispaniola!

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:15.220
Helm to starboard!

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:29.120
<i>Driven by the storm, the Hispaniola cut through the waves!</i>

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:33.080
<i>It was great, I felt revived!</i>

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:37.710
<i>The storm made us forget
the death of First Mate Arrow.</i>

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:58.780
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest....

00:15:58.780 --> 00:16:01.810
Careful, Jim, you're gonna fall in
the water if you move too much.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:05.020
No, I won't!
This storm is nothing!

00:16:05.850 --> 00:16:07.850
Then help me peel these potatoes.

00:16:07.850 --> 00:16:10.730
After the storm, they'll all be hungry.

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:12.190
Okay, I'll help!

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:19.450
Yo-ho-ho and a bottle of rum!

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:23.690
Drink and the devil had d—

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:27.570
Strange. There are fewer waves all of a sudden.

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:28.380
Y-You're right.

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:46.030
Captain!

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:48.230
A ghost ship!

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:22.970
It's First Mate Arrow!

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:24.560
Yes, it's really him!

00:17:30.890 --> 00:17:33.990
L-Look...
It's like he's beckoning someone.

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:42.910
What is it Mr. Arrow?
Who are you beckoning?!

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:56.910
It's Silver!
Yes, he's beckoning Silver!

00:17:57.410 --> 00:18:00.290
It's a curse!
Mr. Arrow really has been murdered.

00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:02.610
And Silver is the murderer!

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:04.090
You know what they say.

00:18:04.090 --> 00:18:06.570
When a man is murdered at sea,

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:11.150
his ghost returns to search for the murderer and take him away to the other world.

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:13.480
Silver!

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:20.450
What are you talking about?
It's just a superstition.

00:18:20.850 --> 00:18:22.490
Superstition, my boot!

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.730
If you refuse to go...

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:26.910
...we will all sink with the ship!

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:28.650
What, are you for real?

00:18:28.650 --> 00:18:31.880
Absolutely!
We're all done for!

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:33.880
Stop your whining!

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:38.260
Rest assured. I just have to accept his invitation and board that ship.

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:43.810
Hey, Puppy!

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:46.250
Stop trembling and bring down the rowboat!

00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:49.020
Silver, you can't go!
Stay here!

00:18:49.020 --> 00:18:53.640
Hey now, Jim... You think
that I killed Mr. Arrow, too?

00:18:54.850 --> 00:18:57.850
If I'm taken to the other world,
that means you were right.

00:18:57.850 --> 00:19:00.200
But I'm going to return, you can believe me.

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:16.730
Hey, look at that!

00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:19.730
The rowboat is moving without being rowed!

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:21.050
Silver!

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:20.530
Listen to me, Mr. Arrow.

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:22.780
I, John Silver,

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:26.970
do not believe in God,
the devil or superstition.

00:20:43.770 --> 00:20:47.650
Look...
The ghost ship lost its glow.

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:41.600
<i>The ghost ship sunk.</i>

00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:44.000
<i>A while later,</i>

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:47.720
<i>the Hispaniola came out of the terrible storm.</i>

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:56.500
Silver.

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:57.210
Yes?

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:58.830
I...

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:02.800
Although it may just have been for a bit...
I'm sorry that I doubted you.

00:22:04.070 --> 00:22:07.880
Say, Silver. When you were aboard the ghost ship,

00:22:07.880 --> 00:22:09.140
weren't you afraid?

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:13.810
I wonder... I can hardly remember what I was feeling at the time.

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:22.360
I'm more afraid of this little knife
than some ghost ship.

00:22:23.330 --> 00:22:25.090
You ol' prankster!

00:22:27.100 --> 00:22:31.240
To      be        continued

00:22:32.450 --> 00:22:37.490
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:32.450 --> 00:22:37.490
Hey sea breeze

00:22:37.490 --> 00:22:43.300
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:37.490 --> 00:22:43.300
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:44.520 --> 00:22:49.510
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:44.520 --> 00:22:49.510
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:49.510 --> 00:22:54.950
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:49.510 --> 00:22:54.950
A word to my dear mother

00:22:54.950 --> 00:23:00.360
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:54.950 --> 00:23:00.360
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:05.820
kaban ippai no

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:05.820
And that my bag filled

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:11.450
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:11.450
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:11.450 --> 00:23:17.310
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:11.450 --> 00:23:17.310
Will be brought back

00:23:18.400 --> 00:23:23.900
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:18.400 --> 00:23:23.900
The sunset on my back

00:23:23.900 --> 00:23:29.790
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:23.900 --> 00:23:29.790
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:39.510
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:39.510
I blow out a whistle

00:23:44.460 --> 00:23:47.730
Just my luck!
I've been kidnapped.

00:23:47.730 --> 00:23:49.740
During our stop at the port,

00:23:49.740 --> 00:23:52.680
I'm separated from the others so
some Englishmen call out to me,

00:23:52.680 --> 00:23:54.620
but they turn out to be kidnappers!

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:56.740
A the ship must soon depart,

00:23:56.740 --> 00:24:00.540
Silver comes to my rescue,
but is shot with a pistol!

00:24:00.900 --> 00:24:03.950
C'mon, tell me...
What am I going to do?!

00:24:04.900 --> 00:24:07.550
Next time on Treasure Island:
"Kidnapping In the Slave Port"

00:24:07.550 --> 00:24:12.550
m 0 0 l 960 0 960 720 0 720

00:24:07.550 --> 00:24:12.550
*

00:24:07.550 --> 00:24:12.550
Next time

00:24:07.550 --> 00:24:12.550
Coming soon!

00:24:07.550 --> 00:24:12.550
Kidnapping
In The Slave Port

00:24:08.220 --> 00:24:10.100
What would you do in my place?
